Harbor: a Direct2D bitmap shared from another bitmap can be drawn (#93).

CreateSharedBitmap, given bitmap properties, set the new bitmap's options to TARGET | CANNOT_DRAW for everything
that isn't a DXGI surface, an ID2D1Bitmap source included. Such a bitmap gets no shader view, and drawing it
draws nothing. Excel shares its tile bitmaps this way: with hardware acceleration off its grid and ribbon came
out black or empty. The shared bitmap now has its source's options, as it already did when no properties were
given.

Test: WindowsTests/d2d/run.sh.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -420,6 +420,10 @@
         memcpy(&bitmap_desc, desc, sizeof(*desc));
         if (IsEqualIID(iid, &IID_IDXGISurface) || IsEqualIID(iid, &IID_IDXGISurface1))
             bitmap_desc.bitmapOptions = d2d_get_bitmap_options_for_surface(data);
+        else if (IsEqualIID(iid, &IID_ID2D1Bitmap) && data)
+            /* HARBOR HACK: a bitmap shared from another bitmap can be used the way its source can. Marked
+             * "cannot draw" it got no shader view, and drawing it gave black (#93). */
+            bitmap_desc.bitmapOptions = unsafe_impl_from_ID2D1Bitmap(data)->options;
         else
             bitmap_desc.bitmapOptions = D2D1_BITMAP_OPTIONS_TARGET | D2D1_BITMAP_OPTIONS_CANNOT_DRAW;
         bitmap_desc.colorContext = NULL;
